      "message": "1. The tests are done on target platform Qemu using phosphor-logging utils log-create with the extend option.\ne.g log-create xyz.openbmc_project.State.CPER.Fatal \\\n  -j \u0027{\"SOURCE\":\"/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system/board/MB\",\"CPER\":\"{}\"}\u0027 \\\n  --extend xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER.Processed \\\n  \u0027{\"DiagnosticDataType\":\"xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.CPER.Types.ContentType.CPER\",\"NotificationType\":\"8f87f311-c998-4d9e-a0c4-fb4dfc2c8c14\",\"SectionType\":\"\",\"Oem\":{\"XYZ\":\"{\\\"@odata.type\\\":\\\"#XYZ_LogEntry.v1_0_0.XYZ_LogEntry\\\",\\\"HardwareRegisters\\\":[{\\\"RegisterName\\\":\\\"SMN_STATUS\\\",\\\"Address\\\":\\\"0x03B00054\\\",\\\"Value\\\":\\\"0xXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\\\"},{\\\"RegisterName\\\":\\\"MCA_STATUS\\\",\\\"Address\\\":\\\"0x00000401\\\",\\\"Value\\\":\\\"0xXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\\\"}],\\\"XYZFieldIdentifiers\\\":[{\\\"ERRORID\\\":12016,\\\"Description\\\":\\\"Compute Tray Error\\\"}],\\\"RackUnitPosition\\\":\\\"XYZ:RACK_ID\\\"}\"}}\u0027 \\\n  --extend xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER.Raw \\\n  \u0027{\"Data\":[68,80,69,82,1,0,255,255,18,52,86,120,170,187,204,221]}\u0027\n2. This will create dbus entry for the event with extension interfaces attached.\nThe corresponding entries in bmcweb EventLog and CPERRawLog service is checked.\n3. There are couple of tests done using busctl call to CPER processor service(builds which has CPER processor integrated)\n4. Apart from this the regular bmcweb CI tests are run locally",
